      "modify_to": "If occlusion leaves an object needed for localization genuinely underconstrained after using the available calibrated views and visible geometry, move upward to a clear viewing height while retaining any held cube, then re-localize. Do not make this recovery motion merely because the wrist view crops the object or part of it is hidden."
    }
  ],
  "refused": "The mandatory two-camera reconstruction introduced in round 2 is replaced by a hierarchy permitting geometrically constrained single-view reconstruction: this round establishes that requiring correspondences caused unnecessary recovery motions when current front-view geometry was usable. Its geometric-center, reprojection, and no-invented-height safeguards remain. No fixed color priority, nearest-cube ranking, left/right preference, future target list, or scene-specific coordinates are added; all three rounds leave exact new-target selection unresolved. No yaw-history field, hard-coded yaw branch, remembered bin coordinates, or fixed numerical rim height is added. Current geometry can recover the bin, and no general yaw-selection convention was established. Existing top-face localization needs no duplicate instruction. Existing deposit-count annotations remain unchanged; held_color supplies missing release-color evidence without changing completed-release timing."
